  <p>
    Auto locksmith work is callout-driven and often urgent, which makes it easy for the admin side — invoicing, job
    history, what was actually fitted — to fall behind the work itself. GarageCloud treats a locksmith callout as a
    normal job on the <a href="/features/workshop-board">workshop board</a>, so it's tracked the same way as any
    other piece of <a href="/garage-management-software">garage management</a> work.
  </p>

  <h2>What matters for locksmith jobs specifically</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>VRM lookup to confirm vehicle details fast, on site, before starting the job.</li>
    <li>A record of what was fitted or programmed against the vehicle, for warranty and future reference.</li>
    <li>Invoicing raised from the completed job, sent before leaving the customer.</li>
    <li>Ghost immobiliser fitting and warranty records kept alongside key and lock work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Warranty and history, not just the callout</h2>
  <p>
    A locksmith callout often isn't a one-off — a customer who's had a lock changed or a key reprogrammed may come
    back with a related issue months later. Keeping that history against the vehicle, rather than in a paper
    invoice book, means the next job starts with context instead of from scratch. See <a href="/pricing">pricing</a> for which plan fits.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
